      "writtenOn": "2026-07-24T16:45:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think `sets it to \"false\"` should be included. Reading the [`gitattributes` manpage](https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/docs/gitattributes.html#_diff), a string value for `diff\u003d\u003cstring\u003e` is interpreted as the diff driver to use. So I think `diff\u003dfalse` looks for a diff driver named `\"false\"` in gitconfig. Obviously Gerrit won\u0027t use any external diff driver, but I think we should just keep our current behavior in that case and ignore those attributes.\n```suggestion\n    // or the \"binary\" macro which JGit expands to \"-diff -merge -text\").\n    boolean isBinary \u003d diffAttr !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 diffAttr.getState() \u003d\u003d Attribute.State.UNSET;\n```",
      "range": {
